{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":58885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041a6ae992b20a7a5f5f316c966a7d97","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now build 02_Apple_ID_Sheet (sheet over 01_Welcome): dimmed welcome + sheet. I'll build frame 02 at x=450, y=1000.\n\nLayout: frame 393x852. Dim overlay: full-screen black 40%. Sheet: white rounded-24 top corners, height ~520 anchored bottom (y=852-520=332). Content: grabber; Logo_Meet centered top; \"Apple ID\" title 22 Bold center; body text center (multi-line): 'Do you want to sign in to Meet Dating App: Meet People with your Apple ID \"sarahp@example.com\"?' — with email maybe plum; Face ID button (primary gradient, white, with Icon_Face_ID + \"Face ID\"); close (Icon_Close) at top-right of sheet; status bar over dimmed; home indicator white inside sheet.\n\nFor \"sheet over 01_Welcome\": should the frame contain the welcome behind dimmed? Visually nicer. But duplicating welcome content is heavy. I'll include a simplified dimmed backdrop — actually easiest and most accurate: clone frame 01 (W.clone()) as background inside frame 02? A frame can't contain another top-level frame clone as child — yes it can: clone W, append into frame02, then overlay dim. That gives genuine \"sheet over 01_Welcome\". Then remove the duplicate's status bar (it'll be under dim anyway). Let's do: \n- frame02 = figma.createFrame 393x852, clip.\n- bg = W.clone(); page.appendChild(bg)? Clone lands as sibling; then frame02.appendChild(bg), set x=0,y=0. But bg has its own status bar/home indicator — fine under dim.\n- dim rect black 0.45.\n- sheet frame.\n- status bar on top (white glyphs? dimmed background dark → status bar glyphs black barely visible; recolor to white: set fills of its children vectors/text to white).\n\nPrototype: bg is a clone; fine.\n\nSheet details: y=332 height=520, cornerRadius top 24 (Figma supports cornerRadius per corner via topLeftRadius etc.), white, shadow upward.\n\nContents:\n- grabber: 40x5 rounded, LINE color, centered y=344.\n- close icon top-right x=341,y=352 (24px, TER color in circle? plain).\n- Logo_Meet centered 56x57 at y≈380.\n- \"Apple ID\" 22 Bold centered y≈450.\n- Body 15 Regular SUB centered, width 300, y≈486, line height 140%: 'Do you want to sign in to Meet Dating App: Meet People with your Apple ID \"sarahp@example.com\"?'\n- Face ID button: primary gradient 345x52 at y≈600 centered x=24: Icon_Face_ID white 20 + \"Face ID\" white SemiBold 16 centered.\n- home indicator at bottom (y=818) black bar ok on white sheet.\n\nPrototype links: Face ID button → 03_Explore (navigate). close → back. Sheet frame itself: I'll add reaction on Face ID button node.\n\nThen 03_Explore at x=900,y=1000. Content (may scroll; I'll make frame 393x852 showing top portion; brief says may scroll vertically — keep 852 height with content clipped, tab bar visible).\n\nExplore layout:\n- Status bar.\n- Header/Explore instance at y=54 (height 64). Actually component h=64; place y=54 → occupies to 118.\n- Stories row: horizontal, y=126, height 90. \"Your Story\" + Ben, Lucie, Marry, Claire, Lina, Jo, Henry, Pierre — 9 avatars; screen shows ~5.5 (64px each + gap 14). I'll add all 9 in a horizontal strip frame with clipsContent, width 393, padding-left 16. Overflow hidden — fine, shows it's scrollable. Name labels: names. Claire story is prototype link → 05.\n- Buttons row y=228: two buttons \"Make Friends\" (primary small?) and \"Search Partners\" (secondary). Width: (353-12)/2=170 each, x=20,202. Height 40. Make Friends = gradient solid white text; Search Partners = outline plum text? Both pill radius 20.\n- Feed: cards at y=284: FeedPost instance (353x452) at x=20; three posts: Noemi (full), Yu Jian partially visible, Maddison further. With frame height 852 and tab bar at bottom (83 → y=769), visible feed area 284..769 = 485 → first post full + start of second. I'll place second at 284+452+16=752 (partially visible behind tab bar). Third at 752+468 → offscreen; still include for \"may scroll\" completeness? Extra children clipped; I'll include all three to show scrollable content; fine.\n\nEach FeedPost instance: set Name text, Meta text, replace avatar image? Avatar inside instance is photoBox frame inside instance — I can't easily change inner image instance. Hmm — FeedPost component uses Noemi avatar & Post_Noemi_Slater photo. For Yu Jian/Maddison posts, instances would show wrong photos, and I can't swap instance internals.\n\nAlternative: make FeedPost component with generic placeholders and on screens build feed posts manually per person (photoBox + texts) — but component reuse suffers. Better: make FeedPost a component whose avatar/photo are instances of portrait/post components; Figma supports **instance swap** — but photos are frames containing instances, not direct instances... To enable swapping, put the portrait instance directly in FeedPost (no wrapper frame) with fixed size — portraits would be 120x180 ratio; avatar 40x40 needs cover crop which wrapper provides.\n\nCompromise: build feed posts manually on the screen (not via FeedPost component instance) but ALSO keep FeedPost component in library as the reusable definition. Component reuse criterion: I'll use components where practical; for per-person media, manual builds are necessary since instances can't swap media content. Actually! I CAN swap: the photoBox wrapper contains an INSTANCE of the portrait component. In a FeedPost instance, that nested instance can be swapped via swapComponent! Nested instance swap is allowed: instance.findOne → it's an INSTANCE node; call swapComponent(targetComponent). Yes, that works on nested instances.\n\nSo: on screen, fpInst = FeedPost instance; find nested instance of Portrait_Noemi_Slater → swapComponent(Portrait_Yu_Jian). Then need resize/crop adjust: wrapper is 40x40 clip; swapped instance is 120x180 → scale to cover: after swap, resize to cover and center. Swapped instance keeps prior size (124x180 scaled?) — the wrapper had instance sized to 40x40-cover (i.e., 27x40? originally 120x180 scaled by max(40/120,40/180)=0.333 → 40x60 centered, y offset -10). After swap to 120x180 portrait, new instance will be 40x60 too (swap preserves size) — same ratio (all portraits 120x180), so fine. Some portraits are 270x180 (Maddison, Ben, Henry landscape). Swap preserves instance size; ratio differs → crop wrong but still fills? Instance 40x60 of a 270x180 image scales the whole image (it stretches? No—instance resize scales children/image proportionally? Actually resizing an instance stretches image fill non-uniformly). Acceptable? The avatar wrapper clips to 40x40. A 40x60 instance of landscape image: image stretched to 40x60 → distortion. Hmm.\n\nSafer: after swap, normalize: set instance width/height proportional: given wrapper WxH and image comp cWxcH: s=max(W/cW,H/cH); resize(cW*s,cH*s); center. I'll write a helper swapPhoto(instNode, newCompId, wrapperW, wrapperH).\n\nSimilarly post photo: wrapper 353x300; Post_Noemi 263x180; swapped to Post_Yu_Jian 269x180 etc. Normalize after swap.\n\nGrid cells: same approach — GridCell instances with swap for each Claire_0X/Sarah_0X. Or simpler: build grid cells manually via photoBox per media (they're just media thumbnails + optional play icon). Since GridCell component exists in library, on-screen manual cells replicate it; reuse criterion partially met. I'll use GridCell instances with swaps for correctness where ratio allows, normalizing after swap. Media ratios vary widely (120x180, 270x180, 320x180, 288x180, 101x180, 144x180, 151x180, 135x180, 319x180). Swap+normalize handles all. OK.\n\nStories: Story/Default instances with swap portrait + rename label. Ratios: story avatar 56x56; portraits 120x180 (most), Ben/Henry 270x180 landscape, Marry 180x180. Normalize after swap. Good — component reuse with correct media.\n\nProfile tab bar avatar: Profile is Sarah portrait 26x26 — already Sarah, fine.\n\nSwipeCard: John top; behind stack: 5 more cards each photoBox of Dan/Aidan/William/Keven/Kalvin with scale/translate offsets. Top card = SwipeCard instance (John data already default). Behind cards: simple rounded photo cards, progressively smaller/y-offset: card2 scale 0.94 y+12, card3 0.89 y+22, card4 y+30, card5 y+36, card6 y+40 with increasing darkness overlay.\n\nGiven frame height 852: card area between header (~110) and action buttons (~700). Card 345x436 at x=24,y=130. Behind stack visible at bottom edges. Action buttons at y≈600? Card bottom 566. Buttons row y=600 (64px buttons: pass, superlike smaller 52, like). Tab bar overlay at bottom y=769 over everything.\n\nHmm buttons y=600, 64 tall → ends 664, tab bar top 769. OK.\n\nLet me now write screen 02.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"40768603-5f91-4a43-90ea-486ebdcb8b36","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:53:34.185Z","thinking_duration_ms":65847}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":58885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041a6ae992b20a7a5f5f316c966a7d97","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Welcome looks good. Now I'll build 02_Apple_ID_Sheet as a sheet over a dimmed clone of Welcome."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"80d03a63-1eda-4982-91a0-54968196a24b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:53:35.760Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":58885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041a6ae992b20a7a5f5f316c966a7d97","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_7b5d4ea4","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','Bold','Extra Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:s})));\nconst PLUM={r:0.2941,g:0.0863,b:0.298};\nconst INK={r:0.10,g:0.086,b:0.11}, SUB={r:0.435,g:0.408,b:0.455}, TER={r:0.63,g:0.60,b:0.655};\nconst LINE={r:0.929,g:0.906,b:0.937};\nconst solid=(c,o=1)=>({type:'SOLID',color:c,opacity:o});\nconst gradBrand=()=>({type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR',gradientTransform:[[0.5,0.866,0],[-0.866,0.5,1]],gradientStops:[{position:0,color:{r:0.2941,g:0.0863,b:0.298,a:1}},{position:1,color:{r:0.8667,g:0.5333,b:0.8118,a:1}}]});\nconst shadow=(y,b,o=0.14)=>({type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.1,g:0.02,b:0.11,a:o},offset:{x:0,y},radius:b,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'});\nfunction txt(str,size,style,color){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:'Inter',style};t.characters=str;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[solid(color)];return t;}\nasync function iconInst(id,size,color){\n  const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=c.createInstance();i.resize(size,size);\n  if(color){i.findAll(n=>['VECTOR','BOOLEAN_OPERATION','ELLIPSE','RECTANGLE','STAR','POLYGON','LINE'].includes(n.type)).forEach(v=>{v.fills=[solid(color)];v.strokes=[];});}\n  return i;\n}\nconst F=figma.createFrame();F.name='02_Apple_ID_Sheet';F.resize(393,852);F.x=460;F.y=1000;F.fills=[solid({r:1,g:1,b:1})];F.clipsContent=true;page.appendChild(F);\n\n// dimmed welcome backdrop\nconst W=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('16:30');\nconst bg=W.clone();F.appendChild(bg);bg.x=0;bg.y=0;\nbg.findOne(n=>n.name==='Status Bar').visible=false;\nbg.findOne(n=>n.name==='Home Indicator').visible=false;\nconst dim=figma.createRectangle();dim.name='Scrim';dim.resize(393,852);dim.fills=[solid({r:0.06,g:0.02,b:0.07},0.55)];F.appendChild(dim);\n\n// sheet\nconst sheet=figma.createFrame();sheet.name='Sheet';sheet.resize(393,520);sheet.x=0;sheet.y=332;\nsheet.fills=[solid({r:1,g:1,b:1})];\nsheet.topLeftRadius=24;sheet.topRightRadius=24;sheet.bottomLeftRadius=0;sheet.bottomRightRadius=0;\nsheet.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.06,g:0.02,b:0.07,a:0.35},offset:{x:0,y:-8},radius:32,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];\nsheet.clipsContent=true;\nF.appendChild(sheet);\n\nconst grab=figma.createRectangle();grab.name='Grabber';grab.resize(40,5);grab.cornerRadius=2.5;grab.fills=[solid(LINE)];grab.x=176.5;grab.y=10;sheet.appendChild(grab);\nconst close=await iconInst('5:23',22,TER);close.name='Icon/Close';close.x=353;close.y=24;sheet.appendChild(close);\nconst logo=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:4')).createInstance();logo.resize(54,55);logo.x=169.5;logo.y=52;sheet.appendChild(logo);\nconst t1=txt('Apple ID',22,'Bold',INK);t1.textAutoResize='HEIGHT';t1.textAlignHorizontal='CENTER';t1.resize(393,t1.height);t1.y=124;sheet.appendChild(t1);\nconst body=txt('Do you want to sign in to Meet Dating App: Meet People with your Apple ID “sarahp@example.com”?',15,'Regular',SUB);\nbody.name='Body';body.lineHeight={value:150,unit:'PERCENT'};body.textAlignHorizontal='CENTER';body.textAutoResize='HEIGHT';body.resize(310,100);body.x=41.5;body.y=168;sheet.appendChild(body);\n// Face ID button\nconst fb=figma.createFrame();fb.name='Button/FaceID';fb.resize(345,54);fb.x=24;fb.y=318;fb.cornerRadius=27;fb.fills=[gradBrand()];fb.effects=[shadow(8,16,0.25)];sheet.appendChild(fb);\nconst fi=await iconInst('5:73',22,{r:1,g:1,b:1});fi.x=24;fi.y=16;fb.appendChild(fi);\nconst fl=txt('Face ID',16,'Semi Bold',{r:1,g:1,b:1});fl.textAutoResize='HEIGHT';fl.textAlignHorizontal='CENTER';fl.resize(345,fl.height);fl.y=18;fb.appendChild(fl);\n\n// status bar (white glyphs) + home indicator\nconst sb=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:33')).createInstance();sb.x=0;sb.y=0;F.appendChild(sb);\nsb.findAll(n=>['VECTOR','RECTANGLE'].includes(n.type)&&n.name!=='Dynamic Island').forEach(v=>{v.fills=[solid({r:1,g:1,b:1})];});\nconst t941=sb.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT');if(t941)t941.fills=[solid({r:1,g:1,b:1})];\nconst hi=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:44')).createInstance();hi.x=0;hi.y=818;F.appendChild(hi);\nreturn {frame:F.id};\n","description":"Build 02_Apple_ID_Sheet with dimmed Welcome backdrop, bottom sheet, logo, copy, Face ID button and close","fileKey":"5xY0YjB6IWmTqgOsns9U6t"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"3a39f57e-ed7f-4990-bd07-5014768d7841","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:54:16.803Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_7b5d4ea4","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
