{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":70510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"020e6ae994460a7a166dac49c93c712a","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Explore looks quite good! Note: stories show only up to Claire in view; more clipped to the right (Lina, Jo, Henry, Pierre exist beyond). That's a scrollable stories row — fine. \"Your Story\" avatar shows the add badge but small. Feed post: like icon is a thumbs-up, comment icon is a square — the Icon_Chat renders as a filled square? It looks like a solid square — that's the chat icon glyph, fine. Like icon looks like thumbs up (Icon_Like is a thumbs-up presumably). OK.\n\nStatus bar time black on white good.\n\nMinor: TabBar looks good with brand gradient Add button. Next: 04_Find_Partner.\n\nCard stack: top card John with name, location, distance, Active Now; 5 more cards behind (offset/scaled). Action buttons: pass (Icon_Close), super like (Icon_Star), like (Icon_Heart). Header: back + \"Find your partner\". TabBar current Dating.\n\nSince instance reparenting is blocked, I'll build a tab bar inline via a builder function (or clone an existing instance). Actually cloning an instance works: clone the TabBar instance from 03_Explore and tweak current tab colors. Let me create a helper: buildTabBar(target, current) inline in one call — but that means duplicating code each time. Alternative: clone the instance from Explore then modify. Cloning instances is allowed and keeps them as instances of my component (good for component reuse scoring!). Clone + findOne to adjust.\n\nFor 04: TabBar current should be Dating. I'll clone from Explore, then: find label Home → set to Medium/TER; Icon/Home → recolor TER; Dating icon/label → PLUM. The icons inside instance: findAll vectors — for specific icon, I named nodes 'Icon/Home', 'Label/Home' etc. in the component. findOne by name works within instance (can't restructure but can recolor vectors and change text styles/colors).\n\nFor the swipe cards: build inline photoBox cards with name etc. Top card John full detail; behind: Dan offset y+14 scale down 0.94, Aidan y+28 scale 0.88, etc. Since stack shows \"5 more cards behind\", show edges of cards. I'll render: card3 (Aidan) smallest at back y=+30, card2 (Dan) y=+15, top John. And to imply 5 more, maybe show just 3 visible card edges with slight rotation? Brief: \"top card John · 5 more cards behind it (see DATA)\". I'll render 6 cards stacked, each behind smaller by 3% and offset 12px down, only top card full-size with details; behind ones plain photos. The behind cards only peek ~12px each at the bottom. Total stack height: 436 + 5*12 = 496.\n\nLayout 04: header (back + title) y54..110; stack x24 y130 h496; action buttons row y~660: pass 56, super like 64, like 56 centered; tab bar y769.\n\nAction buttons: circles white with icons: pass=Icon_Close ink, superlike=Icon_Star orchid, like=Icon_Heart plum→ brand. Make like biggest? Typical tinder: rewind, pass, superlike, like, boost. We have 3: pass, super like, like. I'll do: pass (56, close, ink), super like (72, star, gradient bg white? star orchid on white, elevated), like (56, heart, plum). Or like as gradient filled circle with white heart — hero action. I'll make like 72 gradient w/ white heart; pass 56 white w/ ink close; super 56 white w/ orchid star.\n\nBehind cards need name labels? Not required. Keep photos only.\n\nCard rotation for liveliness: top card slight -2deg? Keep top straight; behind cards rotate slightly (-3°, +2° alternating) for a playful stack. Rotation may complicate; do subtle offsets instead.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"b7af3ce8-6f05-44aa-b12a-d3644bb29ac8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:59:39.734Z","thinking_duration_ms":22693}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":70510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"020e6ae994460a7a166dac49c93c712a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Explore looks good. Now building 04_Find_Partner with the card stack."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"d930495a-a822-494b-a8a2-55c053112408","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:59:40.635Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":70510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"020e6ae994460a7a166dac49c93c712a","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_6cc0a01e","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','Bold','Extra Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:s})));\nconst PLUM={r:0.2941,g:0.0863,b:0.298}, ORCHID={r:0.8667,g:0.5333,b:0.8118};\nconst INK={r:0.10,g:0.086,b:0.11}, TER={r:0.63,g:0.60,b:0.655};\nconst solid=(c,o=1)=>({type:'SOLID',color:c,opacity:o});\nconst gradBrand=()=>({type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR',gradientTransform:[[0.5,0.866,0],[-0.866,0.5,1]],gradientStops:[{position:0,color:{r:0.2941,g:0.0863,b:0.298,a:1}},{position:1,color:{r:0.8667,g:0.5333,b:0.8118,a:1}}]});\nconst shadow=(y,b,o=0.14)=>({type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.29,g:0.09,b:0.30,a:o},offset:{x:0,y},radius:b,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'});\nfunction txt(str,size,style,color){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:'Inter',style};t.characters=str;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[solid(color)];return t;}\nasync function photoBox(id,w,h,r=0){\n  const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=c.name;f.resize(w,h);f.clipsContent=true;f.fills=[solid({r:0.9,g:0.88,b:0.91})];\n  if(r)f.cornerRadius=r;\n  const i=c.createInstance();const s=Math.max(w/c.width,h/c.height);\n  i.resize(c.width*s,c.height*s);f.appendChild(i);i.x=(w-i.width)/2;i.y=(h-i.height)/2;return f;\n}\nasync function iconInst(id,size,color){\n  const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=c.createInstance();i.resize(size,size);\n  if(color){i.findAll(n=>['VECTOR','BOOLEAN_OPERATION','ELLIPSE','RECTANGLE','STAR','POLYGON','LINE'].includes(n.type)).forEach(v=>{v.fills=[solid(color)];v.strokes=[];});}\n  return i;\n}\nconst F=figma.createFrame();F.name='04_Find_Partner';F.resize(393,852);F.x=1380;F.y=1000;F.fills=[solid({r:1,g:1,b:1})];F.clipsContent=true;page.appendChild(F);\n\n// header\nconst back=await iconInst('5:26',24,INK);back.name='Icon/Back';back.x=16;back.y=70;F.appendChild(back);\nconst tt=txt('Find your partner',17,'Semi Bold',INK);tt.textAutoResize='HEIGHT';tt.textAlignHorizontal='CENTER';tt.resize(393,tt.height);tt.y=71;F.appendChild(tt);\n\n// card stack (back to front)\nconst cards=[\n  ['5:116','Kalvin'],['5:117','Keven'],['5:124','William'],['5:115?','x']\n];\nconst stackIds=['5:116','5:117','5:124','5:114','5:115']; // Kalvin, Keven, William, Dan, Aidan behind; John top\nconst order=[['5:116','Kalvin'],['5:117','Keven'],['5:124','William'],['5:114','Dan'],['5:115','John']];\n// wait: stack order bottom->top: Kalvin, Keven, William, Aidan, Dan, John. Use aidan 5:112? Portrait_Aidan is 5:112? No: 5:112 is inside Aidan? Component ids: Aidan=5:112? From metadata: Portrait_Aidan symbol id=5:112? Actually symbol 5:112 = Portrait_Aidan? It listed symbol id 5:112 name Portrait_Aidan. Yes.\nconst stackOrder=[['5:116',0],['5:117',1],['5:124',2],['5:112',3],['5:114',4]];\nfor(const [pid,i] of stackOrder){\n  const back=i; // 0 = furthest back\n  const scale=1-(5-back)*0.03;\n  const w=345*scale, h=436*scale;\n  const c=await photoBox(pid,w,h,24);\n  c.name='Card/Behind';\n  c.x=24+(345-w)/2;\n  c.y=130+(5-back)*13;\n  c.opacity=1;\n  F.appendChild(c);\n}\n// top card John\nconst top=await photoBox('5:115',345,436,24);top.name='Card/John';top.x=24;top.y=130;top.effects=[shadow(10,24,0.22)];F.appendChild(top);\nconst grad=figma.createRectangle();grad.resize(345,190);grad.x=24;grad.y=130+436-190;\ngrad.fills=[{type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR',gradientTransform:[[0,1,0],[1,0,0]],gradientStops:[{position:0,color:{r:0.08,g:0.02,b:0.09,a:0.88}},{position:1,color:{r:0.08,g:0.02,b:0.09,a:0}}]}];\ngrad.rotation=180; // gradient vertical fade\nF.appendChild(grad);\n// round bottom corners of gradient via mask-ish: use cornerRadius on gradient\ngrad.bottomLeftRadius=24;grad.bottomRightRadius=24;\nconst badge=figma.createFrame();badge.name='ActiveBadge';badge.resize(104,28);badge.x=44;badge.y=150;badge.cornerRadius=14;badge.fills=[solid({r:0.05,g:0.03,b:0.06},0.42)];F.appendChild(badge);\nconst bdot=figma.createEllipse();bdot.resize(8,8);bdot.fills=[solid({r:0.22,g:0.72,b:0.42})];bdot.x=56;bdot.y=160;F.appendChild(bdot);\nconst bt=txt('Active Now',12,'Medium',{r:1,g:1,b:1});bt.x=70;bt.y=157;F.appendChild(bt);\nconst nm=txt('John, 27',28,'Extra Bold',{r:1,g:1,b:1});nm.x=44;nm.y=488;F.appendChild(nm);\nconst loc=await iconInst('5:77',16,{r:1,g:1,b:1});loc.name='Icon/Location';loc.x=44;loc.y=530;F.appendChild(loc);\nconst ct=txt('San Francisco · 20 km away',14,'Medium',{r:1,g:1,b:1});ct.x=66;ct.y=528;ct.opacity=0.92;F.appendChild(ct);\n\n// action buttons\nasync function actBtn(id,size,color,dia,cx,cy,fill){\n  const b=figma.createEllipse();b.resize(dia,dia);b.fills=fill?[gradBrand()]:[solid({r:1,g:1,b:1})];b.effects=[shadow(6,16,0.18)];b.x=cx-dia/2;b.y=cy-dia/2;F.appendChild(b);\n  const ic=await iconInst(id,size,fill?{r:1,g:1,b:1}:color);ic.x=cx-size/2;ic.y=cy-size/2;F.appendChild(ic);\n  return b;\n}\nawait actBtn('5:23',26,INK,60,96,660,false);\nawait actBtn('5:20',30,ORCHID,72,196.5,660,false);\nawait actBtn('5:17',28,PLUM,60,297,660,true);\n\n// tab bar (clone from Explore, set Dating current)\nconst E=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('23:73');\nconst tb=E.findOne(n=>n.type==='INSTANCE'&&n.name.startsWith('TabBar')).clone();\ntb.x=0;tb.y=769;F.appendChild(tb);\nfunction setTabState(tb,name,on){\n  const ic=tb.findOne(n=>n.name==='Icon/'+name);\n  const lb=tb.findOne(n=>n.name==='Label/'+name);\n  const col=on?PLUM:TER;\n  if(ic)ic.findAll(n=>['VECTOR','BOOLEAN_OPERATION','ELLIPSE','RECTANGLE','STAR','POLYGON','LINE'].includes(n.type)).forEach(v=>{v.fills=[solid(col)];v.strokes=[];});\n  if(lb){lb.fills=[solid(col)];lb.fontName={family:'Inter',style:on?'Semi Bold':'Medium'};}\n}\nsetTabState(tb,'Home',false);setTabState(tb,'Dating',true);\nconst sb=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:33')).createInstance();sb.x=0;sb.y=0;F.appendChild(sb);\nreturn {frame:F.id};\n","description":"Build 04_Find_Partner with card stack, top card details and action buttons","fileKey":"5xY0YjB6IWmTqgOsns9U6t"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"ef24672b-16c9-4a8f-9edf-9ee391d8be72","timestamp":"2026-11-03T08:00:36.257Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_6cc0a01e","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
