{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":704,"estimated_tokens_delta":1,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"96195692-04b7-414d-9be3-3fe3303999e7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":83344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040e6ae995bd0a7a5e6f638c987a4db9","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Almost all icons are stroke-based — recoloring strokes is needed, not fills. My iconInst cleared strokes and set fills, which means icons are currently invisible everywhere except fill-based ones (play, more)! In the screenshots... the bell rendered on Explore? Looking back at the Explore screenshot, I see bell at top right... Actually yes, small dark bell visible. Hmm, that means setting v.fills worked? For stroke-based icons, setting fills adds a fill in addition to existing strokes. I set v.strokes=[] which removed strokes, leaving fill... which would fill the open path weirdly. But bell appeared fine-ish at small size.\n\nAnyway, icons currently get `fills=[color]` and `strokes=[]` — for stroke icons the result may look broken/filled. Looking at screenshots: back arrow on 04 looks fine? It's barely visible in screenshot. The heart in tab bar Dating renders as filled heart (looked fine). Hmm, actually in tab bar screenshot the icons looked okay because fill covered the shape outline.\n\nBut this is fragile. Better approach: set both fills and strokes to the color, preserving strokeWeight. Let me fix iconInst behavior globally by patching all icon instances in workspace: iterate over all instances of icon components within my frames, and set strokes=[color] matching their current fill color.\n\nPlan: walk workspace frames; for each node that is an instance of an Icon_* component, find vector descendants; read current fills color (if any) else default; set strokes=[that color] and fills=[] for stroke-based icons... but how do I know which are stroke-based vs fill-based in the instance? Use the main component's vector: check original component vector stroke count. Map componentId -> strokeBased. For instances, mainComponent gives id.\n\nFor stroke-based icons: v.strokes=[solid(color)], v.strokeWeight=orig strokeWeight (keep), v.fills=[] (clear the fill I added). For fill-based (play, more): fills=[color], strokes=[].\n\nThe color to use: current fill color of vector (what I set). If no fills, default INK.\n\nStatus bar instances: skip (not icons).\n\nLet me write the fix pass.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"837efe4f-890d-478a-9617-9f1347a313ff","timestamp":"2026-11-03T08:05:49.753Z","thinking_duration_ms":13725}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":83344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040e6ae995bd0a7a5e6f638c987a4db9","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_2d53bfc0","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\nconst solid=(c,o=1)=>({type:'SOLID',color:c,opacity:o});\nconst strokeBased=new Set();\nasync function mark(id){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const vs=c.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR');if(vs.length&&vs.every(v=>(v.strokes||[]).length>0))strokeBased.add(id);return id;}\n// preload classification by component id\nconst comps=['5:26','5:23','5:70','5:29','5:51','5:58','5:54','5:77','5:63','5:67','5:33','5:48','5:45','5:42','5:17','5:20','5:36','5:39','5:81','5:85','5:88','5:91','5:97','5:101','5:105'];\nfor(const id of comps) await mark(id);\nlet fixed=0;\nfor(const frame of page.children){\n  if(frame.type!=='FRAME'||frame.name==='Meet — Components')continue;\n  const insts=frame.findAll(n=>n.type==='INSTANCE');\n  for(const inst of insts){\n    const mc=await inst.getMainComponentAsync();\n    if(!mc)continue;\n    if(!comps.includes(mc.id))continue;\n    const isStroke=strokeBased.has(mc.id);\n    const vecs=inst.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR');\n    for(const v of vecs){\n      const cur=(v.fills&&v.fills[0]&&v.fills[0].color)?v.fills[0].color:{r:0.10,g:0.086,b:0.11};\n      const op=(v.fills&&v.fills[0]&&v.fills[0].opacity!==undefined)?v.fills[0].opacity:1;\n      if(isStroke){v.strokes=[solid(cur,op)];v.fills=[];}\n      else{v.fills=[solid(cur,op)];v.strokes=[];}\n      fixed++;\n    }\n  }\n}\nreturn {fixed, strokeIcons:[...strokeBased].length};\n","description":"Fix icon recoloring: move color to strokes for stroke-based icons across all workspace screens","fileKey":"5xY0YjB6IWmTqgOsns9U6t"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"513a9f10-ab65-403d-bded-4eac99536de5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T08:06:04.078Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_2d53bfc0","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
