{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":86518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02206ae996380a7af4cc5b177044ea35","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — the topmost behind card (Dan, index 4) at y=119 with height 436*0.97=423 — top card at y=130. Dan's top edge at 119, top card covers 130-566, so an 11px sliver of Dan shows above the card. But Dan's top edge is within the header area (title at y~71-90). y=119 is below the title (~90) fine. Kalvin at y=75, top edge overlaps the title zone (title at y=71, height ~21 → ends 92). Kalvin is only 293 wide, centered → x=50..343. It might visually collide with title text edges. Hmm, title is centered text; at y 75-92 it could overlap Kalvin's card top corners. Reduce offsets: use -(5-i)*9 → Kalvin y=130-45=85, still overlapping slightly. Or start stack at y=150: keep top at 130; offsets 9: tops at 121,112,103,94,85. The title baseline ~71-92. Kalvin top edge 85 < 92 → tiny overlap with title area but title text is centered horizontally; Kalvin card spans x 50-343, so under the title text it could show behind \"Find your partner\". Not great.\n\nAlternative: move whole stack down: top card y=140, offsets 10 → tops 130,120,110,100,90. Title ends ~92 → Kalvin at 90 overlaps 2px. Acceptable-ish. Or reduce scale steps: scale 1-(5-i)*0.025, offset (5-i)*9. Kalvin: scale .875 → w=302, y=130-45=85.\n\nHmm. Simpler: shift stack down and trim: top card y=138, h=428 (to keep bottom at 566). Behind tops: offset 9 → 129..93. Title ends ~92. OK barely.\n\nActually cleanest: title zone ends at ~94 (back icon at y70 h24 → 94). Make Kalvin top ≥ 96: offsets: top=138, behind tops: (5-i)*8 → 130,122,114,106,98. Stack visual fine.\n\nLet me set: top card y=138, gradient/badge/text move +8. Behind offsets 8. Action buttons stay.\n\nAlso the status bar: Explore screenshot status bar looks fine.\n\nAnother thing on 04: Active Now badge renders nicely. The pass star colors ok. Tab bar Dating current good.\n\nLet me apply the +8 shift to stack items (badge 150→158, name 488→496, loc 530→538, city 528→536, grad y, top card y).","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"4cebfa17-3cad-41df-ac57-b4a2c28a2001","timestamp":"2026-11-03T08:07:55.935Z","thinking_duration_ms":18843}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":86518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02206ae996380a7af4cc5b177044ea35","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_1f21b5b3","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst F=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('24:114');\nconst backs=F.children.filter(n=>n.name==='Card/Behind');\nbacks.forEach((c,i)=>{c.y=138-(5-i)*8;});\nconst top=F.findOne(n=>n.name==='Card/John');top.y=138;\n// gradient rect is the one with GRADIENT_LINEAR fill at frame level\nconst grad=F.children.find(n=>n.type==='RECTANGLE'&&n.fills&&n.fills[0]&&n.fills[0].type==='GRADIENT_LINEAR');\ngrad.y=138+436-190;\nconst badge=F.findOne(n=>n.name==='ActiveBadge');badge.y=158;\n// green dot ellipse inside frame level\nconst dot=F.children.find(n=>n.type==='ELLIPSE'&&n.fills[0]&&n.fills[0].color&&n.fills[0].color.g>0.5);if(dot)dot.y=168;\nfor(const t of F.children.filter(n=>n.type==='TEXT')){\n  if(t.characters==='Active Now')t.y=165;\n  if(t.characters==='John, 27')t.y=496;\n  if(t.characters.startsWith('San Francisco'))t.y=536;\n}\nconst loc=F.children.find(n=>n.name==='Icon/Location');if(loc)loc.y=538;\nreturn {ok:true};\n","description":"Shift top card and its overlay down 8px, tighten stack offsets","fileKey":"5xY0YjB6IWmTqgOsns9U6t"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8da9f8-6f65-452e-96bf-8860e9b0c5f8","uuid":"d93cfa5c-2df3-4a5d-ad4f-4eaa93be60eb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T08:08:06.203Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_1f21b5b3","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
